# A universally quantified rule with fresh mothers
#
# A rule says that each human has some mother, and Tom and Ann are humans.
# Explicit N3 quantifiers distinguish the universally bound person from a
# fresh existential witness in the conclusion: eyemind concludes that Tom
# and Ann each have a mother, two different unnamed individuals.

@prefix : <http://example.org/> .

# :x is declared universal, so the rule applies to every human. Inside the
# conclusion, @forSome makes :y existential: each firing gets a fresh mother.
@forAll :x .
{
    :x a :Human
} => {
    @forSome :y .
    :x :hasMother :y
} .

# The humans.
:tom a :Human .
:ann a :Human .
